# Allow-list, not deny-list.
#
# A deny-list only protects paths someone remembered to name. This repo
# previously ignored the key by filename pattern while leaving source_data/
# — which holds the raw exports with farmer names, GPS coordinates and
# village names — unignored, one `git add -A` away from publication.
#
# Everything is ignored by default. Publishable paths are named explicitly.

*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE

!data/
!data/*.csv

!docs/
!docs/*.md

!scripts/
!scripts/*.py

# Belt and braces: these must never be committed even if a rule above is
# later loosened.
source_data/
previous_release/
private/
*_CONFIDENTIAL.*
*pond_key*
*pond_id_mapping*
private_config.py
export-*.csv
.DS_Store
